source: crates/spt-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: out
---
Permanent SSH2/SSH3 tunnels with reconnect, observability, and service integration.

Usage: spt [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  config      Manage configuration files (init, validate, diff, render, reload)
  profile     Manage SSH/SSH3 tunnel profiles
  forward     Manage forwards (local/remote TCP, UDP)
  tunnel      Run, inspect, and control tunnels
  service     Install and control native services
  key         Generate, inspect, and install SSH keys
  secret      Manage the secret vault and OS keychain references
  auth        Authentication helpers
  dns         Built-in DNS resolver and hosts-file management
  firewall    Inspect and manage OS firewall / packet-filter rules
  log         Log tailing, sink testing, and export
  observe     Metrics and Windows Event Log helpers
  event       Event bindings and sinks
  stats       Statistics summaries and live counters
  session     Inspect and manage active sessions
  ftp         FTP→SFTP translator service
  sftp        SFTP file operations and mount planning
  diagnose    Targeted diagnostics and support bundles
  benchmark   Controlled benchmarking against forwards
  mcp         Built-in MCP server controls
  status      Show overall app status — daemon, tunnels/profiles, forwards, and subsystems (status
              API, MCP, DNS, metrics, remote-config, events, services)
  status-api  Controls for the read-only HTTP status API
  completion  Generate shell completions
  about       List bundled libraries and their licenses
  kill        Terminate every running `spt` instance on this host
  update      Embedded auto-updater (off by default). Manual commands work regardless of the
              `[updater].enabled` flag; the background polling thread is only spawned when
              explicitly enabled
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to a single config file
          
          [env: SPT_CONFIG=]

      --config-dir <PATH>
          Path to a directory of `*.toml` configs (loaded in lexical order)

      --config-url <URL>
          HTTPS URL of a remote config to fetch
          
          [env: SPT_CONFIG_URL=]

      --config-fingerprint <SHA256>
          SHA-256 fingerprint pin for `--config-url`

      --state-dir <PATH>
          Override the runtime state directory
          
          [env: SPT_STATE_DIR=]

      --portable
          Portable mode: keep all runtime state next to the executable instead of OS-standard
          locations (no OS install required).
          
          `main.rs` performs a raw pre-clap scan of the argv for this flag so portable paths are
          resolved before the runtime is built; this declaration exists so the flag is visible to
          `--help`, generated shell completions, and the man pages.

      --profile <NAME>
          Restrict operations to the named profile

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format for command results

          Possible values:
          - human: Human-readable text (default)
          - json:  Structured JSON
          - jsonl: JSON Lines (one record per line)
          - yaml:  YAML
          
          [default: human]

      --json
          Convenience alias for `--output json`

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Tracing log level

          Possible values:
          - error: Only errors
          - warn:  Warnings and above
          - info:  Informational and above (default)
          - debug: Debug and above
          - trace: Trace and above (very verbose)
          
          [default: info]

      --color <COLOR>
          Color policy for human output

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Auto-detect based on tty
          - always: Always emit color escapes
          - never:  Never emit color escapes
          
          [default: auto]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (repeat for more)

      --no-color
          Disable color (legacy convenience flag; use `--color never`)

      --dry-run
          Show what would happen without making changes

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
